Manage the access rules of the buckets of a Nexo server (Admin API,
admin:ManageAccessRules): rules with a priority, an effect (allow or deny),
principals, actions and a pattern of the keys (a prefix, a glob with *, **, ?,
[abc] and {a,b}, or an RE2 regular expression), evaluated by the policy engine
next to the IAM policies and the bucket policy: a deny in any source denies.

Principals: '*' (everyone, anonymous included), user:NAME, group:NAME,
accesskey:KEY, distribution:ID. Actions: read, stream (the videos play as HLS,
the originals cannot be downloaded), list, write, delete, tag, all, or actions
(s3:GetObject, nexo:GetMediaStream). Every change replaces the rules of the bucket
atomically and fails if they changed meanwhile.

Usage:
  nexoctl access [flags]
  nexoctl access [command]

Available Commands:
  block-public Block the public access of the cluster or of a bucket
  export       Export the access rules of a bucket as YAML
  import       Replace the access rules of a bucket with those of a YAML file
  public       Apply and show the public access presets of a bucket
  rule         Add, list, show, remove and reorder the access rules of a bucket
  test         Test the access rules on keys (who may do what)

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for access

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl access [command] --help" for more information about a command.
